[36m(TaskRunner pid=186768)[0m Next, we factorize \(362880\) into its prime factors:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=186768)[0m \[ 9! = 2^7 \times 3^4 \times 5 \times 7 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=186768)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=186768)[0m We need to find the divisors of \(362880\) that have a units digit of 1. These divisors must be congruent to 1 modulo 10. Such divisors must be coprime to 10, meaning they cannot have factors of 2 or 5.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=186768)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=186768)[0m Thus, the divisors must be of the form \(3^b \times 7^c\) where \(0 \leq b \leq 4\) and \(0 \leq c \leq 1\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=186768)[0m 
